# Vulnerabilities that cannot be fixed yet because they are capped by
# transitive dependencies. Each entry documents the blocker and why the
# vulnerable code path is not reachable from this project.

# filelock: Arbitrary file overwrite via insecure database file reopening
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-112940
# Fixed in 4.2.1, but every version of `unstructured` (incl. the latest) pins
# filelock<4.0.0, so the fix cannot be pulled in. We do not use filelock
# directly, and the affected database file reopening is not exercised.
CVE-2026-112940 exp:2027-04-30

# transformers: save_pretrained path traversal allows arbitrary file writes
# through chat template names
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-9856
# Fixed in 5.10.0, but the version is capped at <5.6 by optimum-intel 2.2.0
# (required by sentence-transformers[openvino]), so the fix cannot be pulled in.
# We do not call save_pretrained with user-controlled chat template names.
CVE-2026-9856 exp:2027-04-30

# transformers: unauthorized file write via
# GenerativePreTrainedModel.load_custom_generate()
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-80047
# No fixed version is published yet, and the version is in any case capped at
# <5.6 by optimum-intel 2.2.0 (required by sentence-transformers[openvino]).
# We never call load_custom_generate / GenerativePreTrainedModel.
CVE-2026-80047 exp:2027-04-30

